{
  "name": "Bass Bloom",
  "notes": "The field itself gets bigger on the hit. `ScaleWarp` says `zoom > 1 makes the shape bigger`, so an envelope on `zoom` from 1.0 to 2.8 magnifies the noise about the centre -- features grow outward and off both ends, then shrink back. Nothing translates, nothing new is drawn. It is one number.\n\nWhy an envelope and not the band directly, when `27-subwoofer` uses the band: a follower gives you the envelope of the MUSIC and this wants the envelope of the HIT. `expo_out` at a 5 ms attack snaps out and eases back, which is a bloom; the raw band wobbles with every partial in the bass note and the field would shimmer rather than pulse.\n\nThe chain is `M2 -> M3.rate` -- the drift clock accelerates on every hit, so the field does not merely swell, it LURCHES forward and settles, which is what gives a bloom direction. A second warp under the first tiles the field, and the tile count is on the envelope too at a small negative depth: on a hard hit the repeats merge into one large form and separate again as it decays. Cerise through violet to cobalt, 100 degrees of analogous run, with a single acid lime at the far end that only the fully bloomed field reaches.",
